# Profile "no-uidplus" (scripts/profiles.sh, README.md "iCloud-fidelity profiles").
# Sourced by bash and parsed by scripts/verify-profiles.mjs: plain KEY=value / KEY="value" lines only.
#
# The "icloud" profile without UIDPLUS: no MOVE, no SPECIAL-USE, no UIDPLUS. imapflow then cannot use
# UID EXPUNGE, so messageMove() and messageDelete() finish with a plain EXPUNGE, which purges EVERY
# \Deleted message in the mailbox. This is the path the MCP server's expunge guard (SPEC 2.4) must catch.
PROFILE_DESCRIPTION="no MOVE, no SPECIAL-USE, no UIDPLUS: moves/deletes end in a plain EXPUNGE"
PROFILE_IMAP_PORT=3143
PROFILE_IMAPS_PORT=3993
PROFILE_SPECIAL_USE=no
# Same as the icloud profile minus UIDPLUS. Note that Dovecot still implements UIDPLUS: it keeps sending
# APPENDUID/COPYUID response codes and accepts UID EXPUNGE if a client sends it anyway.
PROFILE_CAPABILITY="IMAP4rev1 QUOTA LITERAL+ NAMESPACE CHILDREN BINARY UNSELECT SORT CATENATE ESEARCH ESORT THREAD=ORDEREDSUBJECT THREAD=REFERENCES CONDSTORE ENABLE QRESYNC CONTEXT=SEARCH WITHIN SASL-IR SEARCHRES ID IDLE"
